! Open Phases

`LarOpenPhase` names ten vessel boot phases in declaration order, from `boot` to `live` (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/lararium-vessel.ts`). Both node and browser composers pass phase callbacks through the shared keel (`packages/lararium-node/src/open-node-vessel.ts`; `packages/lararium-browser/src/open-browser-vessel.ts`).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/sequence`>>

!! Phase Sequence

The type declares this order (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/lararium-vessel.ts`):

```text
boot → repo-open → catalog-ready → island-ready → wiki-ready → draft-ready
→ vessel-ready → tw5-booted → corpus-ready → live
```

Node emits `boot`, `repo-open`, and `catalog-ready` while opening its repository and catalog (`packages/lararium-node/src/open-node-vessel.ts`); browser emits the same three (`packages/lararium-browser/src/open-browser-vessel.ts`). Shared `assembleVessel` emits `island-ready` after the island handle and composite layers stand, then `corpus-ready` after `loadCorpora` completes (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/open-vessel-core.ts`).

The shared wiki cap emits `wiki-ready` and `vessel-ready` after `mountWikiSlot`; the shared mount cap emits `tw5-booted` and `live` after `mountPrimaryWiki` (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/core-caps.ts`). `mountWikiSlot` resolves the draft handle, but these caps emit no `draft-ready` (`core-caps.ts`). The resulting full-vessel callback order places `corpus-ready` before `wiki-ready`, despite its later place in the type declaration (`open-vessel-core.ts`; `core-caps.ts`).

A canon crossing into `@crossroads` passes `lares meme promote --approval <file>`; the charter's seats approve the exact carrier bytes before the move (`packages/lares-cli/src/commands/meme-promote.ts`; <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/kahu`>> #/chartered-classes).

<<~/ahu>>

